# Google Drive & Sheets sync credentials.
#
# IMPORTANT: this app is a static site with no build step and no server, so nothing
# actually reads a .env file at runtime — browsers can't load .env files directly, and
# there's no bundler here to inject these into the shipped JS. This file exists purely
# as a familiar, standard reference for the values you need.
#
# The values that actually matter are read from js/google-config.js at runtime instead:
#   1. Copy js/google-config.example.js to js/google-config.js
#   2. Fill in the same two values shown below
#   3. Commit it — GitHub Pages only serves what's in the repo, and neither value here is
#      meant to be kept private (see the comment in js/google-config.js). If you'd rather
#      keep them out of git history anyway, .gitignore the file and inject it at deploy
#      time instead (e.g. a GitHub Actions secret).
#
# See README.md → "Google Drive & Sheets sync" for how to obtain them, and why a real
# secret (a Client Secret, or a service-account key) is intentionally NOT part of this
# setup and must never go in this file — this app authenticates as *you*, via your own
# Google sign-in, rather than holding a credential that could be extracted from the browser.

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY
